#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120676} :activity/id #uuid "045805f2-d7d9-501d-8e4b-541e2bb65e50" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048315 :topic/id #uuid "93e6a7ce-2e63-5dea-bbbb-a00575db5770" :topic/math-academy-id 1852} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120676 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121035 :tutorial/content "Given two vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ the set of all possible linear combinations of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is\n\n$$\nU = \\left\\{ x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{a}_2 \\: : \\: x_1,x_2\\in\\mathbb{R} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe set $U$ is also called the **linear span** of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ and is denoted by $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}.$ We say that $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ are the **generators** of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}.$\n\nFor example, let's find the linear span generated by the following vectors:\n![](images/55/55c749dccc54c252b9120f148e383f395c09fb4cd4bec0e1cce8ed441ecb6199.svg)\n\nFrom the definition of linear span, we know that if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ then $\\mathbf{b}$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = x_1\\mathbf{a_1} + x_2\\mathbf{a_2}\n$$\n\n for some $x_1,x_2\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the linear span of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is\n![](images/21/2181b471f34906eeaea7889abbba37c797a2f9624cee455b43b00fc048247cd1.svg)\n\nGeometrically, $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}$ can be viewed as the plane $\\Pi$ that passes through the origin and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/d5/d5b202475e0bc3ebb07df1f07bab72e9e74b13a99196c2a8a5adb624a7534a03.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "c4e2e270-f1fb-5633-9239-4696e8f0a25b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3193 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "05c77385-415b-5833-b935-9be3a2038c69" :step/math-academy-id 17469 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120677}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120677 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119619 :question/id #uuid "d5a81b39-421e-55c3-90de-d9f4e6489cd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-4795"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048499}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120303} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120355} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314972} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315058} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315059} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317213} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342223} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421529} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421530}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "74f8be2d-0f86-52de-8277-fd7db395c80d" :step/math-academy-id 17471 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120750}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121036 :tutorial/content "The linear span of vectors can be interpreted geometrically as the points in space that can be reached by adding multiples of those vectors.\n\n- The span of a single nonzero vector is a *line* through the origin. More precisely, if $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0},$ then $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a} \\}$ determines the *line* with direction vector $\\mathbf{a}$ that passes through the origin. For instance, if\n![](images/dd/ddef437718d3a11811da02a17e2207d75e2d1852eeada67ab494af45b2a655e2.svg)\nthen $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a} \\}$ represents the line $l$ *spanned* by $\\mathbf{a}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/08/080aa6203494e915e28c491a3d86176f7ba634bcbdfe40b094c07d85fb29bb69.png)\n\n- The span of two non-parallel vectors is a *plane* through the origin. More precisely, if $\\mathbf{a} \\not\\parallel \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel), then $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}, \\mathbf{b} \\}$ determines the *plane* with direction vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ that passes through the origin. For instance, if\n![](images/1f/1f92378ff1d1409f0928caa4b3ce98861784d0f2aa51dd1eda30e8877a0134ff.svg)\nthen $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}, \\mathbf{b} \\}$  represents the plane $\\Pi$ *spanned* by $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/56/5606535bd91eb35745a9852ceb451720339105f5a97fb66ccfcb1164ecd55ffd.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "c50c93be-7bf2-5511-b456-c60478a53270" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3194 :tutorial/title "Geometric Interpretation of the Linear Span"} :step/id #uuid "15713f7b-cd11-55c3-93fd-8040ac62d36f" :step/math-academy-id 17477 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120679}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120679 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119620 :question/id #uuid "94a17888-dcef-58e0-8147-0dec3745f136" :question/math-academy-id "e-4799"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050308}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120304} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120306} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241021} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241023} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241024} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241025} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317208} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342240} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342241} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342243} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344944} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393417} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399461} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403766} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421528}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"} :step/id #uuid "33abdb88-235d-550f-b5bb-06946454437c" :step/math-academy-id 17478} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120750 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119671 :question/id #uuid "21a6808a-5b1c-5b1d-9bd4-da605fb6d920" :question/math-academy-id "e-6218"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120294} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120516} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241017} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241019} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342228} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342229} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342230} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342231} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342237} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342238} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342239} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421531} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421532} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436138}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "5cca50af-2a48-5696-bc3a-fc57e95232b0" :step/math-academy-id 23264 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120678}}] :activity/title "Linear Span of Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120046}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436139} :activity/id #uuid "a554ac31-b397-5970-b942-0ac30a77ef87" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048315 :topic/id #uuid "93e6a7ce-2e63-5dea-bbbb-a00575db5770" :topic/math-academy-id 1852} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436139 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "711bff2a-6953-5410-bb47-66e0c9bf361e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436132} {:answer/id #uuid "94b9bad3-ee59-5063-a347-e17815281f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436133} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f39043-eded-58ee-8538-d1b96c3a350b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436134} {:answer/id #uuid "a676903a-1471-5d07-b4fb-3436e54d4e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436135} {:answer/id #uuid "caaab5ae-2e33-5881-8499-57baf2a35a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436136}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436132} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4437cfd-d611-50b5-a26a-25a34c0f8218" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1dfec754-9c19-551c-8df7-102df6435813" :question/math-academy-id "q-34636" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-8 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -18 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 10 & k-32\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 10 & k-32\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-2.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-2\\,⟹\\,k=2.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "19ecde81-ba5d-52b8-b7b7-9282a3f95b93" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436142}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436140 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ea0212-0c8f-50de-a9e9-986f267bdb5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339138} {:answer/id #uuid "25b09d72-beeb-56f8-b3c5-bd45509568ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339451} {:answer/id #uuid "392acaa5-a047-5743-bd68-0e133d8bead9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339642} {:answer/id #uuid "c4734975-ddc9-5119-b9e9-59e873e223ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340873} {:answer/id #uuid "d55e6034-4f45-5b74-b206-75e90bc1aef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341016}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339138} :answer-field/id #uuid "690b25a1-892c-577b-b6f7-6ff437d6dcd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e12a2efc-9d88-56c5-96b5-ec530d76269d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74594" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-6.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-6\\,⇒\\,k=6.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "43f3636b-da52-552f-b6cc-fe77773f48fa" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436141}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436141 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "285f60c4-cfc6-509d-a8ca-df316a92348e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238408} {:answer/id #uuid "306f3ae9-9703-5c61-9e1f-a029efeb6fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238477} {:answer/id #uuid "7197f81b-8003-5f00-b98f-69a60e60b685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239030} {:answer/id #uuid "7aef6609-8c36-5411-ba86-81d4a40f69b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239115} {:answer/id #uuid "db09174f-1cdc-5bdb-8120-63756b097fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239966}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186239966} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5dbe15-3666-592c-9f7a-5c21bff9ad15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "edff4129-bf9d-5206-854e-d3e5b43ca237" :question/math-academy-id "q-105253" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,3,2⟩$, $c=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-5,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=5 \\\\ 3s-t &=-5 \\\\ 2s-t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=5 \\\\ t &=2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =5 \\\\ -s+2(2) & =5 \\\\ -s+4 & =5 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$"} :step/id #uuid "70ef282b-5ccd-5b1e-a1f8-1bcffa1e4789" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436143}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436142 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28049f08-5684-5304-ad3d-9f534b59f279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339478} {:answer/id #uuid "67519cd7-cc6e-5952-bf35-4a4a24da747e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340043} {:answer/id #uuid "79c14b9a-0376-5405-a220-fdac02f464da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340214} {:answer/id #uuid "92c70a7d-6a91-5cb6-8d17-c5ff99a5580f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340448} {:answer/id #uuid "b383d39f-e410-5314-b906-611aa1b45702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340760}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340043} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c41871-59a4-56ef-80fe-7d004904e3a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "62066547-f160-5da7-be83-cd71028d6d36" :question/math-academy-id "q-74556" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & k-6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-15\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-15.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-15\\,⇒\\,k=15.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9b5c264f-f673-5283-81e5-4aa5642b7e81" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436140}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436143 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145063fc-8e8e-5c5e-b9c0-4ce50643aeca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238221} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd14ba1-3c05-5721-9490-57e8bf80fea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238742} {:answer/id #uuid "a01540c4-5818-561d-9151-d28aeb0e7fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239452} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e4047e-41ea-50d0-ab94-58e7363cb874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239637} {:answer/id #uuid "ebdd9058-9132-5515-90b7-33b231320d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238742} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dee8bc9-1a1f-59f0-8b66-162d23f34c3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8c4cb4f7-2d57-5ca9-8ffa-a4fe4548b0de" :question/math-academy-id "q-105265" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,-1,4⟩$, $c=⟨-3,-8,14⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-10,-14⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t &=5 \\\\ -s-8t &=-10 \\\\ 4s+14t &=-14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t &=5 \\\\ t &=3 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s-3t & =5 \\\\ -s-3(3) & =5 \\\\ -s-9 & =5 \\\\ s & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-14,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-14b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-14)\\cdot 3=-42.$"} :step/id #uuid "acd92085-628d-5fd7-8ceb-59efc32f4636"}] :activity/title "Linear Span of Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436131}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501294} :activity/id #uuid "9b83a1b4-0764-5c5a-941f-c490395d7bf4" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048315 :topic/id #uuid "93e6a7ce-2e63-5dea-bbbb-a00575db5770" :topic/math-academy-id 1852} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501284 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18285e78-b775-52d3-9ce4-8875b58cd9dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339343} {:answer/id #uuid "1be7024d-e144-5979-8991-a6fe697cbc56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} {:answer/id #uuid "39886f7e-3d38-5ba7-ae30-319ca5a0cc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339646} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3953fd-8be9-5eec-b885-1d99ddc7adf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340246} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9dd147-f938-5d4d-8bda-da9705de4409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340808}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ed9efb-9d03-53c8-9fad-57fa155b57a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55c44296-8bfb-53c1-b37c-07eab30d99a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74598" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,-7,-9⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,-3,-6⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t &=2 \\\\ 2s-7t &=-3 \\\\ 3s-9t &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t &=2 \\\\ -t &=1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-t=1\\,⟹\\,t=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+3t & =2 \\\\ -s+3(-1) & =2 \\\\ -s & =5 \\\\ s & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-5,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-5b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-5)\\cdot (-1)=5.$"} :step/id #uuid "b3f379e0-d96a-59b3-a5f3-cd3157bae58d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501299}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501287 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4823cb09-c970-5693-9e2b-8bd1376d913d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339771} {:answer/id #uuid "80e4ce86-252f-55b0-9c33-fb68673d04ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340284} {:answer/id #uuid "acf2eadb-7cd8-54d4-a9e9-27a5f5fb57dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340703} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c084ff-7550-5511-af3c-c648fa93d138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340987} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a99f2f-8df2-5e11-8059-1ebda3f846e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340987} :answer-field/id #uuid "d24716d5-0fd3-56ef-817c-00602c395b53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1691e3c5-722a-5803-9898-54e9fb9a633f" :question/math-academy-id "q-74559" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2} &=-8 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 10 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 10 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k+6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-18\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-18.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-18\\,⇒\\,k=18.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b72404ac-26bb-566e-86ed-eac8022d2e24" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501284}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501293 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "351d3eaa-8d71-5eaf-91f1-6a15d982842b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238515} {:answer/id #uuid "521c8347-9356-57c0-82a2-f6f058e2fdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238763} {:answer/id #uuid "77e423df-6336-5ebd-a988-70ffd97ff91b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239089} {:answer/id #uuid "9e933237-ff23-52d2-a25d-7ee910ab795d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239441} {:answer/id #uuid "b70c1cd0-e286-53f1-ba39-4e8669a377a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239650}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238763} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca08aa7d-69a4-53e7-9a42-33232fc442bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "847914f8-60db-55a2-9155-7cfe231e6bcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105237" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 12 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+9\\,⇒\\,k=-9.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e2d3f1ac-8edc-511e-a9dc-9a185ba14e65"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501294 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ca81bd-a843-517f-a7ef-72a2701907bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315161} {:answer/id #uuid "31e52722-b368-5c85-8ea5-9c73d21f221f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315408} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3a18e5-9318-5ff6-9f5d-5297ea2e47b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315452} {:answer/id #uuid "43670fca-c17e-5839-b7bf-2ab9ba603b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315509} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0a632c-b0f2-53fa-9828-61b94974deed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315509} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed15606e-311e-585d-8930-70b904dd77b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "725d2e8b-44d5-5b25-872e-7c29b876b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-34212" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,7,-3⟩$, $c=⟨-8,10,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨6,9,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-8t &=6 \\\\ 7s+10t &=9 \\\\ -3s-4t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 10 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{66}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+28{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-8t &=6 \\\\ t &=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-8t & =6 \\\\ s-8(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =6 \\\\ s+4 & =6 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b-\\frac{1}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})=-1.$"} :step/id #uuid "e82061b7-e579-5804-86dd-b377e54a1147" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501287}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501299 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28acedc8-6185-5174-a20f-1523f6e81664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238413} {:answer/id #uuid "911bf0a4-bca6-575a-8b8e-b3222ff2700c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239312} {:answer/id #uuid "aa49ecea-790f-512b-a264-3f8fef658cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239546} {:answer/id #uuid "deff7940-817f-5ec1-8070-a43c35299f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240003} {:answer/id #uuid "e11c88b3-593a-53f2-8807-09f826099a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240003} :answer-field/id #uuid "b832e88e-aa6a-556d-b56a-7bd0240d9f74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4e417e2f-54d8-52fa-a283-38ee2e22e96c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105232" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+8.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+8\\,⇒\\,k=-8.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "fc03f4e8-430f-5ef2-ba85-5ff08877b297" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501293}}] :activity/title "Linear Span of Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500465}]}
